  "question": {
    "text": "Let the mean and variance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;observations be <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math> respectively. Later on, it was observed that two observations were considered as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math> instead of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn></math> respectively. If the correct variance is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>m</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> are coprime, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></math> are coprime, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>n</mi></math> is equal to"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>315</mn></math>",
